# Low-Level DLL Internals & Native Binary Engineering

This skill provides compiler-grade heuristics and reverse-engineering protocols for Windows PE/DLL binaries, assembly instructions, virtual method tables, and native function detours—enabling deep reasoning on low-level binary targets (e.g. S.T.A.L.K.E.R. `xr*.dll`, GTA ASI plugins, Unreal Engine native extensions, DirectX/Vulkan hooks).

---

## 🏛️ PE32 / PE64 Architecture & Address Calculations

### 1. RVA to File Offset Conversion
Addresses in disassembly and headers are **Relative Virtual Addresses (RVA)**, relative to the module Image Base:
$$\text{Virtual Address (VA)} = \text{ImageBase} + \text{RVA}$$

To find the raw disk file offset for a given RVA:
$$\text{File Offset} = \text{RVA} - \text{Section.VirtualAddress} + \text{Section.PointerToRawData}$$

### 2. Fast PE Header & Export Inspection (Python `pefile`)
```python
import pefile

pe = pefile.PE("target.dll")
image_base = pe.OPTIONAL_HEADER.ImageBase

# Map all exports with RVA, VA, and File Offset
if hasattr(pe, "DIRECTORY_ENTRY_EXPORT"):
    for exp in pe.DIRECTORY_ENTRY_EXPORT.symbols:
        name = exp.name.decode() if exp.name else f"ord_{exp.ordinal}"
        rva = exp.address
        va = image_base + rva
        offset = pe.get_offset_from_rva(rva)
        print(f"[{exp.ordinal}] {name}: RVA=0x{rva:08X} VA=0x{va:08X} FileOffset=0x{offset:08X}")
```

