## 🧬 VTable & C++ Class Layout Reconstruction

In MSVC-compiled binaries, any class with virtual methods starts with a pointer to its Virtual Method Table (`vptr`):

```text
Object Memory Layout:
[+0x00] vptr ───► [0x00] VirtualMethod0 (often destructor)
                  [0x04] VirtualMethod1
                  [0x08] VirtualMethod2
                  [0x0C] VirtualMethod3
[+0x04] MemberVar1
[+0x08] MemberVar2
```

### Identifying VTable Calls in Disassembly
When you observe assembly like:
```asm
mov ecx, [ebp-0x08]       ; ecx = this pointer
mov edx, [ecx]            ; edx = vptr
call dword ptr [edx+0x14] ; call vtable index 0x14 / 4 = 5 (6th virtual method)
```
* **Disassembly Offset:** `0x14`
* **VTable Slot:** $0x14 \div 4 = 5$ (32-bit) or $0x28 \div 8 = 5$ (64-bit).
* **Reconstructed C++ Interface:**
  ```cpp
  class IEngineTarget {
  public:
      virtual void Method0() = 0; // 0x00
      virtual void Method1() = 0; // 0x04
      virtual void Method2() = 0; // 0x08
      virtual void Method3() = 0; // 0x0C
      virtual void Method4() = 0; // 0x10
      virtual void TargetMethod(int arg1, float arg2) = 0; // 0x14
  };
  ```

