## 🪝 Native Detour Hooking & Trampolines

### 1. 5-Byte Relative Jump Hook Blueprint
To hook a function at `TargetAddress` and divert execution to `HookFunction`:
1. Calculate relative jump offset:
   $$\text{Rel32} = \text{HookFunction} - (\text{TargetAddress} + 5)$$
2. Back up the original 5 bytes ("stolen bytes").
3. Make memory writable: `VirtualProtect(TargetAddress, 5, PAGE_EXECUTE_READWRITE, &oldProtect)`.
4. Write opcode `0xE9` followed by the 4-byte `Rel32`.
5. Restore original protection.

### 2. MinHook Integration Template
```cpp
#include <windows.h>
#include "MinHook.h"

// Define original function prototype
typedef int(__thiscall* tEngineRender)(void* thisPtr, int renderFlags);
tEngineRender oEngineRender = nullptr;

// Hook detour function
int __fastcall hkEngineRender(void* thisPtr, void* edx, int renderFlags) {
    // Custom pre-render logic here
    
    // Call original function via trampoline
    int result = oEngineRender(thisPtr, renderFlags);
    
    // Custom post-render logic here
    return result;
}

void InstallHooks() {
    MH_Initialize();
    uintptr_t targetAddr = (uintptr_t)GetModuleHandleA("xrEngine.exe") + 0x4A120;
    MH_CreateHook((void*)targetAddr, (void*)&hkEngineRender, (void**)&oEngineRender);
    MH_EnableHook((void*)targetAddr);
}
```

